1. The open format — Apache License, Version 2.0
------------------------------------------------

The following are licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(full text: ./LICENSE-APACHE, SPDX: Apache-2.0):

  - schema/            the Blueprint schema itself (the format definition)
  - examples/          example blueprints
  - docs/              documentation, including the Schema Atlas
  - tools/validator/   the reference conformance validator
  - tools/doc-snippet-validate/  validates the YAML examples inside the docs
  - tools/port/        verifies the shipped files against the manifest published
                       with them; it describes no blueprint and reads no model
  - tools/vscode-blueprint/   the editor navigation extension
                              (see its own tools/vscode-blueprint/LICENSE)

The format is meant to be adopted freely. You may use, modify, and redistribute
these parts — including in commercial and proprietary products — under the
terms of the Apache License, Version 2.0.


2. The tooling — Functional Source License 1.1 (ALv2 Future License)
--------------------------------------------------------------------

The following are licensed under the Functional Source License, Version 1.1,
with an Apache 2.0 future grant (full text: ./LICENSE-FSL, SPDX: FSL-1.1-ALv2):

  - tools/model-builder/       the model graph, and the vocabulary typing its edges
  - tools/semantic-checker/    the semantic rule pack
  - tools/quality-gate/        self-description coverage
  - tools/coverage-check/      drift between a model's code_refs and the source tree
  - tools/model-query/         the reuse audit over a built model
  - tools/entity-query/        search before you mint
  - tools/next-id/             typed id allocation
  - tools/build-stamp/         build identity for generated artifacts
  - tools/renderer/            markdown and Mermaid documents
  - tools/schema-update/       versioned model migrations
  - tools/schema-atlas/        the generated schema reference
